.TH proxytrack 1 "@DATE@" "httrack website copier"
.SH NAME
proxytrack \- proxy to serve content archived by httrack website copier
.SH SYNOPSIS
@SYNOPSIS@
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B proxytrack
serves pages already archived by
.BR httrack (1)
without going online. It answers HTTP proxy requests on the first address. It answers ICP queries, such as the ones Squid sends, on the second address. It reads httrack caches
.RI ( hts\-cache/new.zip ,
or the older
.I new.ndx
with
.IR new.dat )
and
.I .arc
files. The archived content can also be browsed under
.I /webdav
on the proxy address.
.PP
With
.IR \-\-convert ,
it merges the archives into a single
.I .zip
cache or
.I .arc
file instead, then exits.
.SH OPTIONS
@OPTIONS@
.SH EXAMPLES
@EXAMPLES@
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.IP HTS_LOG
Set to a number above 0 to print internal statistics on the console.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Errors and warnings are written to the console.
@FOOTER@
.PP
The archives are written by
.BR httrack (1).
